## Component Styling

This project uses the "new-york" style variant with the "neutral" base color and CSS variables for theming, as configured in `components.json`.

🎨 Styling and Tailwind 4 Compatibility
All styles are managed via Tailwind CSS v4.
Ensure postcss.config.js is configured for Tailwind 4.
Theme tokens are set in tailwind.config.ts under theme.extend.
Tailwind 4 requires variables to be defined as :root tokens — shadcn components are preconfigured for this.

🧪 Best Practices
You may customize any component by editing the file under src/components/ui.
Avoid altering the internal logic unless necessary — prefer style and variant overrides.
When creating custom variants or sizes, extend the base component file instead of duplicating it.


✅ Summary
Use only locally installed Shadcn components via @/components/ui.
Add new components with the CLI (npx shadcn@latest add ...).
Fully compatible with Tailwind CSS v4 and PostCSS.
